{"segs": ["PA_ja_216:0.4"], "en": "6. The Fish Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_216:1.1", "PA_ja_216:1.2"], "en": "“Neither does this fire blaze, nor does the stake well-polished;”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_216:1.3", "PA_ja_216:1.4"], "en": "And he whom that fisherwoman imagines me to be has gone to another for pleasure;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_216:2.1"], "en": "it is the fire of passion for him that burns me.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_216:2.2"], "en": "My mind is scorched by the fire;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_216:2.3"], "en": "O masters of the net, release me!", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_216:2.4"], "en": "One who has no desire for sense-pleasures is never slain anywhere.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:51:25Z"},
